course: dictionary
lesson: 10892
title: Viper: a snake and a sneaky person
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A viper is a kind of venomous snake, which means it puts poison into its prey or into a person when it bites. The clues in «Cobras, mambas, vipers and rattlesnakes are the famous ones» show that vipers are one of the famous kinds of snake.
explain: Look at the clues about the fangs: «Vipers have two long hollow fangs at the front that fold back against the roof of the mouth when it closes.» Fangs are long, sharp teeth. Fold back means they lie flat until the snake needs them.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. In old stories, a viper can also be a wicked, treacherous person who betrays others. To check which meaning fits, swap your idea into the sentence. If a snake fits, it is the animal; if a sneaky, untrustworthy person fits, it is the old meaning.
fact: A viper is a kind of venomous snake with long fangs that fold back.
fact: The adder is Britain's only venomous snake, and it is shy and protected.
fact: «Pit vipers», such as rattlesnakes, have heat-sensing pits on their faces, so they can find a warm mouse in total darkness.
fact: If someone is bitten by a snake, they should stay calm, keep still and get medical help at once.
fact: Old-fashioned: a viper is a wicked, treacherous person who betrays others.
exercise: «Vipers have two long hollow fangs at the front that fold back against the roof of the mouth.» What are fangs? | Eyes that see in the dark | *Long, sharp teeth used to put venom into prey | Small hairs on the tongue | Scales on the back
exercise: «Rattlesnakes and other pit vipers have two heat-sensing pits on their faces, so they can find a warm mouse in total darkness.» What do the pits help the snake do? | *Sense heat, so it can find warm prey in the dark | Change colour | Taste the air | Hear the wind
exercise: A friend is bitten by a viper. What should you do first? | Wait until tomorrow to see if it gets better | Suck out the venom with your mouth | *Stay calm, keep still and get medical help at once | Run off to catch the snake
test: In an old story, «a viper in the nest» means what? | A nest made of grass | *A dangerous, deceitful person | A bird that sings sweetly | A lost pet
test: What is special about the adder? | It lives in the sea | It has no fangs | *Britain's only venomous snake, and shy and protected | The biggest snake in the world
exam: Why do a viper's fangs fold back? | So they can be seen from far away | So the snake can chew its food | *So they lie flat against the roof of the mouth until the snake needs them | So they grow longer every year
